{title: Save The Last Dance for Me}
{subtitle: Writers: Doc Pomus and Mort Shuman (1960), Artist: Emmylou Harris (1979)}
{comment:  Recommended strum: Island Strum with a "fan" on 2 (d- Fu -u du)}
{comment:  Intro}
[G7]    [G7]    [C]    [C]    

{comment:  Verse 1}
You can [C] dance ... every dance with the guy
Who gave you the eye, let him [G7] hold you tight.
You can [G7] smile, every smile for the man
Who would treat you right, beneath the [C] pale moonlight

